    "created_at": "2019-12-21T21:33:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-12-21T21:33:30Z",
    "body": "WhatsApp, Youtube, Slack and many more would benefit from some punctuation characters being directly accessible for formatting / markup:\n\n- `@`: ping, mention \n- `#`: tag\n- `_`: emphasis (underline, italic) \n- `*`: emphasis (bold) \n- `` ` ``: code (fixed width) \n- `~`: edit (strike-through) \n- `:`: emoji shortcode\n\nNote, this is not enough for markdown, wiki, HTML, BBCode etc. [LWL](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightweight_markup_language) ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
